1e:["$","p","3",{"children":["To stand out during campus placements and product firm drives, your Spring Boot projects must address actual enterprise concerns: **ACID transaction guarantees**, **thread concurrency**, **idempotency**, and **containerized deployment**."]}]
1f:["$","hr","4",{"style":{"borderColor":"var(--border-subtle)","margin":"1rem 0"}}]
20:["$","h2","5",{"style":{"fontSize":"var(--text-2xl)","color":"var(--text-primary)","marginTop":"1.5rem","marginBottom":"0.5rem"},"children":"The Architecture Standard Interviewers Look For"}]
21:["$","p","6",{"children":["When evaluating a backend candidate, top software engineering interviewers look for three specific competency layers:"]}]
22:["$","p","7",{"children":["1. **Data Integrity Under Concurrency**: Do you understand what happens when two users attempt to transfer funds or book the last seat on a flight at the exact same millisecond? Candidates who understand **pessimistic row locking (`SELECT FOR UPDATE`)** and **isolation levels** immediately score higher.\n2. **Network Resilience & Idempotency**: If a client's network drops during an HTTP POST transfer and the user clicks 'Submit' twice, does your server process two payments? Implementing **Idempotency Keys** is standard practice in production.\n3. **Modern Microservice Decoupling**: Rather than dumping everything into one monolithic controller, separating concerns into auth, domain logic, and immutable audit ledgers signals production maturity."]}]
23:["$","hr","8",{"style":{"borderColor":"var(--border-subtle)","margin":"1rem 0"}}]
24:["$","h2","9",{"style":{"fontSize":"var(--text-2xl)","color":"var(--text-primary)","marginTop":"1.5rem","marginBottom":"0.5rem"},"children":"Recommended Project Spotlight: Cloud-Native Banking Engine"}]
25:["$","p","10",{"children":["If you want a project that covers all three criteria, we strongly recommend implementing our **Cloud-Native Banking & Transaction Engine**."]}]
26:["$","p","11",{"children":["This project gives you immediate discussion depth during interviews:\n- Explaining why monetary values are stored in atomic cents/paise rather than IEEE floating-point doubles.\n- Demonstrating row-level locks on PostgreSQL tables to guarantee zero balance anomalies.\n- Showcasing Spring Security 6 stateless JWT tokens with role-based access control (RBAC)."]}]
27:["$","p","12",{"children":["Explore our complete, step-by-step implementation guide including architecture diagrams, SQL schemas, and code samples."]}]
28:["$","hr","13",{"style":{"borderColor":"var(--border-subtle)","margin":"1rem 0"}}]
29:["$","h2","14",{"style":{"fontSize":"var(--text-2xl)","color":"var(--text-primary)","marginTop":"1.5rem","marginBottom":"0.5rem"},"children":"Key Viva & Technical Interview Questions to Prepare"}]
2a:["$","p","15",{"children":["Be ready to answer questions like:\n- *What is the difference between `@Transactional` rollback on checked vs unchecked exceptions?*\n- *How do you prevent database deadlocks when executing reciprocal transfers between accounts?*\n- *Why use JWT over session cookies in a distributed microservice cluster?*"]}]
2b:["$","p","16",{"children":["Having concrete answers rooted in your project architecture turns an intimidating viva into an impressive engineering discussion."]}]
